\section{Areal spatial fields}{


\code{icar(graph)}, \code{bym2(graph, scale_factor)}, \code{car(graph)} and
\code{car_proper(graph)} put a field over the nodes of a symmetric adjacency
matrix \code{graph}. \code{bym2()} computes its \code{scale_factor} from the
graph when it is not supplied. All four accept:

\describe{
\item{\code{group_var}}{Column naming each observation's graph node, when
the graph is over regions rather than rows.}
\item{\code{weight}}{Per-node numeric column turning the field into a
spatially varying coefficient (\code{weight_i * z[node_i]}) instead of an
intercept field. \code{car()} does not take it.}
\item{\code{id}}{Name for the realization, so \code{copy("id")} can share it
with another process.}
}

The umbrella form \code{spatial(~ 1 + w || cell, graph = adj, model = "icar")}
forwards to the same terms and additionally reads a bar, which is how areal
varying coefficients are usually written (see below).
}

\section{Continuous spatial fields}{


\code{gp(lon, lat, ...)} is an NNGP-approximated Gaussian process over
coordinates, \code{multiscale_gp(lon, lat, ...)} a two-scale (local plus
regional) version, and \code{spde(lon, lat, ...)} a Matern field over a
triangular mesh. Coordinates come either from bare column names or from
\code{coords = }, a two-column matrix.

\describe{
\item{\code{cov}}{Covariance function: \code{"exponential"} (default),
\code{"matern"}, \code{"gaussian"}, \code{"spherical"}.}
\item{\code{nu}}{Matern smoothness.}
\item{\code{nn}}{Number of nearest neighbours in the Vecchia
approximation, capped at \code{n - 1}. \code{multiscale_gp()} splits this
into \code{nn_local} and \code{nn_regional}.}
\item{\code{prior_range}}{Length-2 \code{c(r0, alpha)} PC prior on the
range, read as \code{P(range < r0) = alpha}. Required by \code{gp()} and
\code{svc()}, which ship no default; \code{spde()} defaults to
\code{c(0.5, 0.5)} alongside \code{prior_sigma}.}
\item{\code{mesh}, \code{max_edge}, \code{cutoff}}{\code{spde()} mesh
controls, passed to \code{tulpa::spatial_spde()}.}
}
}

\section{Spatially varying coefficients}{


Two terms carry a coefficient that varies over space. They read alike in
prose and are different terms with different coverage.

\strong{Areal}, a weighted bar under the spatial umbrella:

\preformatted{~ 1 + w + spatial(~ 1 + w || cell, graph = adj)}

with \code{method = "nested_laplace"}. One field per bar column, over graph
nodes. Broad family support (single-season, dynamic, integrated and the
community routes) and recovery-tested throughout. This is what most
spatially-varying-coefficient questions want, and it arrives as a
\code{spatial} term, not as \code{svc()}.

\strong{Continuous}, its own term, an NNGP surface over coordinates:

\preformatted{~ elevation + svc(lon, lat, indices = 2, prior_range = c(50, 0.05))}

\describe{
\item{\code{indices}}{Positions of the design columns whose coefficients
vary, read against the design of the arm the surfaces load on. One
surface per entry; index 1 is the intercept.}
\item{\code{coords}}{Two-column coordinate matrix, as an alternative to
bare \code{lon, lat} column names. One coordinate pair per site.}
\item{\code{cov}}{\code{"exponential"} (default), \code{"matern"} or
\code{"gaussian"}.}
\item{\code{nn}}{Nearest neighbours in the Vecchia approximation, default
15, capped at \code{n - 1}.}
\item{\code{prior_range}}{Required, no default: \code{c(r0, alpha)} with
\code{P(range < r0) = alpha}.}
\item{\code{sigma2_prior_scale}}{Scale of the prior on the surface's
marginal variance.}
}

\code{svc()} fits on single-season \code{\link{occu}()} under
\code{"laplace"}, \code{"nested_laplace"} and \code{"nuts"}, and on
\code{\link{removal}()}, \code{\link{distance}()}, \code{\link{fp_occu}()}
and \code{\link{dyn_abun}()} under \code{"laplace"} and
\code{"nested_laplace"}. The surfaces load on the state arm (the occupancy
logit, or log lambda for the count families) and come back as
\code{fit$svc_field}, with the integrated hyperparameters in
\code{fit$svc_hyper}. On any other family, method or arm the term errors and
points at the areal bar rather than being silently dropped.
}

\section{Random effects}{


\code{re(group, ...)} is a grouped random effect, and \code{lme4} bars are
sugar over it: \code{(1 | g)}, \code{(x | g)}, \code{(x || g)},
\code{(0 + x | g)}, \code{(1 | g:h)} and \code{(1 | g/h)} are rewritten to
\code{re()} calls before the formula is evaluated.

\describe{
\item{\code{type}}{\code{"intercept"} (default), \code{"slope"} or
\code{"iid"}.}
\item{\code{covariate}}{Slope column(s): a column name, several names, a
\code{cbind()} matrix or a one-sided formula. Required for
\code{type = "slope"}.}
\item{\code{model}}{Structure over the group levels: \code{"iid"}
(default), \code{"ar1"}, \code{"rw1"}, \code{"rw2"}.}
\item{\code{correlated}}{Whether slopes share a correlated covariance with
the group intercept.}
\item{\code{intercept}}{\code{FALSE} drops the implicit group intercept,
giving a slope-only block.}
}
}

\section{Temporal structure}{


\code{temporal(time, ...)} puts a field over the levels of \code{time}.

\describe{
\item{\code{type}}{\code{"ar1"} (default), \code{"rw1"}, \code{"rw2"} or
\code{"iid"}.}
\item{\code{group}}{Optional grouping, for one series per group.}
\item{\code{cyclic}}{Wraps the last level onto the first.}
\item{\code{tau_shape}, \code{tau_rate}}{Gamma prior on the field
precision.}
}
}

\section{Latent factors and sharing}{


\code{latent(n_factors)} adds per-site latent factors with per-species
loadings to a community model, giving residual co-occurrence.
\code{constraint} and \code{sigma_prior_rate} control the identification
anchor and the loading prior.

\code{copy("id")} shares one realization of the term named \code{id} across
processes, optionally scaled: \code{alpha = 0.5} pins the coupling
amplitude, \code{alpha = grid(c(0.25, 0.5, 1))} marginalizes over it on the
outer integration.
}

\examples{
\dontrun{
# Areal field on occupancy, detection random effect by observer
tobs(occu(), y ~ elev + icar(graph = adj), detection = ~ (1 | observer),
     data = d, visits = v)

# Areal spatially varying coefficient on `year` (the broadly supported form)
tobs(occu(), y ~ year + spatial(~ 1 + year || cell, graph = adj),
     data = d, visits = v, method = "nested_laplace")

# Continuous NNGP varying coefficient on the second design column
tobs(occu(), y ~ elev + svc(lon, lat, indices = 2, prior_range = c(50, 0.05)),
     data = d, visits = v, method = "laplace")
}
}
